{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int N = 266666;\nint n, k, MOD;\nlong long fac[N], inv[N], dp[30][22], arr[18][N], out[N];\n\nlong long modpow(long long a, long long e) {\n    if (e == 0) return 1;\n    long long half = modpow(a, e/2);\n    half = half * half % MOD;\n    if (e & 1) return half * a % MOD;\n    return half;\n}\n\nvoid sos_dp(int idx, int bit) {\n    if (bit >= 17) return;\n    int step = 1 << bit;\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << 17); ++mask) {\n        if (mask & step) arr[idx][mask] += arr[idx][mask ^ step];\n    }\n    sos_dp(idx, bit+1);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &n, &k, &MOD);\n    if (n & 1) {\n        cout << modpow(k, n) << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    fac[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) fac[i] = fac[i-1] * i % MOD;\n    inv[n] = modpow(fac[n], MOD-2);\n    for (int i = n-1; i >= 0; --i) inv[i] = inv[i+1] * (i+1) % MOD;\n    n >>= 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        int pc = __builtin_popcount(i);\n        arr[pc][i] = inv[i*2];\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i) sos_dp(i, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i)\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask)\n            arr[i][mask] %= MOD;\n    int target_pc = __builtin_popcount(n);\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask) {\n        memset(dp, 0, sizeof(dp));\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= k; ++j) {\n            for (int u = 0; u <= 17; ++u) {\n                for (int v = 0; u+v <= 17; ++v) {\n                    dp[j][u+v] += arr[u][mask] * dp[j-1][v];\n                }\n            }\n            for (int v = 0; v <= 17; ++v) dp[j][v] %= MOD;\n        }\n        out[mask] = dp[k][target_pc];\n    }\n    for (int bit = 0; bit < 17; ++bit) {\n        int step = 1 << bit;\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask) {\n            if (mask & step) out[mask] -= out[mask ^ step];\n        }\n    }\n    long long res = (modpow(k, n*2) - out[n] % MOD * fac[n*2] % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n    cout << res << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef modpow(a, e, MOD):\n    if e == 0:\n        return 1\n    half = modpow(a, e // 2, MOD)\n    half = half * half % MOD\n    if e & 1:\n        return half * a % MOD\n    return half\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    MOD = int(data[2])\n    \n    if n & 1:\n        print(modpow(k, n, MOD))\n        return\n    \n    # precompute factorials and inverse factorials up to n\n    fac = [1] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        fac[i] = fac[i-1] * i % MOD\n    inv = [0] * (n + 1)\n    inv[n] = modpow(fac[n], MOD - 2, MOD)\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        inv[i] = inv[i+1] * (i+1) % MOD\n    \n    n >>= 1  # n becomes half\n    max_mask = 1 << 17\n    arr = [[0] * max_mask for _ in range(18)]\n    \n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        pc = bin(i).count('1')\n        arr[pc][i] = inv[i * 2]\n    \n    # SOS DP for each popcount index\n    for idx in range(17):\n        for bit in range(17):\n            step = 1 << bit\n            for mask in range(max_mask):\n                if mask & step:\n                    arr[idx][mask] += arr[idx][mask ^ step]\n        # mod after each idx? In C++ they mod after all SOS, but we can mod after each idx to avoid overflow\n        for mask in range(max_mask):\n            arr[idx][mask] %= MOD\n    \n    target_pc = bin(n).count('1')\n    out = [0] * max_mask\n    \n    for mask in range(max_mask):\n        dp = [[0] * 18 for _ in range(k + 1)]\n        dp[0][0] = 1\n        for j in range(1, k + 1):\n            for u in range(18):\n                for v in range(18 - u):\n                    dp[j][u + v] += arr[u][mask] * dp[j-1][v]\n            for v in range(18):\n                dp[j][v] %= MOD\n        out[mask] = dp[k][target_pc]\n    \n    # inverse SOS\n    for bit in range(17):\n        step = 1 << bit\n        for mask in range(max_mask):\n            if mask & step:\n                out[mask] -= out[mask ^ step]\n    \n    res = (modpow(k, n * 2, MOD) - out[n] % MOD * fac[n * 2] % MOD + MOD) % MOD\n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.71926071238704e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00045253525604493916, -0.0004365683125797659, 0.0, -0.03811095654964447, -0.2523238956928253, -0.00026651646476238966, -1.7046782886609435e-05, -8.34461570775602e-06, -0.0024757706560194492, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0011709030950441957, -0.16022805869579315, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0016039852052927017, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.6689160474925302e-05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.006715585943311453, 0.0, -0.00015686711412854493, 0.0, -6.198863957251888e-06, 0.0, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 